```javascript
function convertToUpperCase(str) {
  let result = '';
  for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {
    // Check if the character is a letter
    if (str[i] >= 'a' && str[i] <= 'z') {
      // Convert the letter to uppercase using ASCII codes
      const upperCaseCharCode = str.charCodeAt(i) - 32;
      result += String.fromCharCode(upperCaseCharCode);
    } else {
      // Add non-letter characters as is
      result += str[i];
    }
  }
  return result;
}
```

This function iterates over each character in the string. If the character is a letter, it converts it to uppercase by subtracting 32 from its ASCII code and then converts the resulting code back to a character. If the character is not a letter, it is added to the result string as is.

