```javascript
function generateRandomString() {
  const characters = "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789";
  const stringLength = 20;

  // Generate a random string of unique characters
  let randomString = '';
  while (randomString.length < stringLength) {
    const randomChar = characters.charAt(Math.floor(Math.random() * characters.length));
    if (!randomString.includes(randomChar)) {
      randomString += randomChar;
    }
  }

  // Calculate the sum of ASCII values
  const sum = randomString.split('').reduce((acc, char) => acc + char.charCodeAt(0), 0);

  // Check if the sum is a prime number
  const isPrime = checkPrime(sum);

  // If sum is not prime, generate a new string recursively
  if (!isPrime) {
    return generateRandomString();
  }

  return randomString;
}

// Function to check if a number is prime
function checkPrime(num) {
  if (num <= 1) {
    return false;
  }

  for (let i = 2; i <= Math.sqrt(num); i++) {
    if (num % i === 0) {
      return false;
    }
  }

  return true;
}

// Generate and print the random string
const randomString = generateRandomString();
console.log(randomString);
```

This program uses a `generateRandomString` function to generate a random string of 20 characters using lowercase letters and numbers. It checks if the sum of ASCII values is a prime number using the `checkPrime` function. If the sum is not prime, it recursively generates a new string until a prime sum is achieved. Finally, it prints the random string to the console.

Here's a recursive JavaScript function that checks if a given string is a palindrome:

```javascript
function isPalindrome(str) {
  // Remove leading and trailing whitespace characters
  str = str.trim();

  // Base case: if the string is empty or only contains one character, it is a palindrome
  if (str.length === 0 || str.length === 1) {
    return true;
  }

  // Convert the string to lowercase for case-insensitive comparison
  const lowerStr = str.toLowerCase();

  // Check if the first and last characters are alphanumeric and equal
  if (isAlphanumeric(lowerStr[0]) && isAlphanumeric(lowerStr[str.length - 1]) && lowerStr[0] === lowerStr[str.length - 1]) {
    // Recursive call: check if the substring between the first and last characters is a palindrome
    return isPalindrome(lowerStr.substring(1, str.length - 1));
  } else {
    return false;
  }
}

// Helper function to check if a character is alphanumeric
function isAlphanumeric(char) {
  return /^[a-zA-Z0-9]+$/.test(char);
}

// Test cases
console.log(isPalindrome("A man, a plan, a canal, Panama")); // true
console.log(isPalindrome("racecar")); // true
console.log(isPalindrome("hello world")); // false
console.log(isPalindrome("12321")); // true
console.log(isPalindrome("not a palindrome")); // false
```

This function takes a string as input and follows the rules mentioned above to determine if the string is a palindrome. It uses recursion to repeatedly check if the first and last characters of the string are alphanumeric and equal, and if so, recursively checks if the substring between those characters is also a palindrome. The function uses a helper function `isAlphanumeric` to check if a character is alphanumeric. The function returns `true` if the string is a palindrome and `false` otherwise.

