Next, it iterates over each element in the input array using a for loop. Inside the loop, it calculates the square root of the current element using the Math.sqrt() method, and then rounds the square root using the Math.round() method. The rounded square root is then pushed into the "result" array.

Finally, the function returns the "result" array, which contains the rounded square roots for each number in the input array.

This implementation has a time complexity of O(n), where n is the length of the input array, because it iterates over each element in the array once to calculate and round the square roots. Additionally, it only uses the Math.sqrt() method once to calculate the square root of each number in the input array, as required.

