    this.account_balance = 0;
    this.transactions = [];
  }

  deposit(amount) {
    if (amount <= 0) {
      throw new Error('Amount must be greater than zero');
    }

    this.account_balance += amount;
    console.log('Updated balance:', this.account_balance);
  }

  withdraw(amount) {
    if (amount <= 0) {
      throw new Error('Amount must be greater than zero');
    }

    if (this.account_balance >= amount) {
      this.account_balance -= amount;
      console.log('Updated balance:', this.account_balance);
    } else {
      throw new Error('Insufficient balance');
    }
  }

  getBalance() {
    return this.account_balance;
  }

  getTransactionHistory() {
    return this.transactions;
  }
}
```

In this implementation, the private variables `account_balance` and `transactions` are initialized in the constructor. The `deposit()` function adds the given amount to the `account_balance` and prints the updated balance. The `withdraw()` function subtracts the given amount from the `account_balance` if the account has enough balance, otherwise it throws an `InsufficientBalanceError`. The `getBalance()` function simply returns the current balance. The `getTransactionHistory()` function returns the `transactions` array.

