- The `sumOfPrimes` function calculates the sum of all the prime numbers in the input array. It iterates through each element in the array and checks if it is a valid number and prime. If it is, the number is added to the sum.
- The `parseFloat` function is used to convert the elements in the array to numbers. If an element cannot be parsed as a number, it will be converted to `NaN`.
- The `isNaN` function is used to check if a number is `NaN`.
