If the array has an odd number of elements, the function returns the middle element of the sorted array by accessing the element at index `Math.floor(length / 2)`.

If the array has an even number of elements, the function calculates the average of the two middle elements by accessing the elements at indices `length / 2 - 1` and `length / 2`, and then dividing their sum by 2.

