```javascript
function deleteExpiredCookies(domain, threshold) {
  // Get all cookies for the given domain
  const cookies = document.cookie.split('; ');

  // Track the number of deleted cookies
  let deletedCount = 0;

  // Iterate over each cookie
  for (let i = 0; i < cookies.length; i++) {
    const cookie = cookies[i];
    const [name, value] = cookie.split('=');

    // Parse the cookie attributes
    const attributes = {};
    const parts = cookie.split('; ');
    for (let j = 1; j < parts.length; j++) {
      const [attrName, attrValue] = parts[j].split('=');
      attributes[attrName.toLowerCase()] = attrValue || true;
    }

    // Check if the cookie belongs to the given domain
    if (attributes.domain) {
      const cookieDomain = attributes.domain.toLowerCase();
      if (!cookieDomain.includes(domain.toLowerCase())) {
        continue;
      }
    }

    // Check if the cookie has an expiration date
    if (attributes.expires) {
      const expiration = new Date(attributes.expires);
      const currentDate = new Date();
      const diffTime = expiration.getTime() - currentDate.getTime();
      const diffDays = Math.ceil(diffTime / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));

      // Check if the expiration date is older than the threshold
      if (diffDays > threshold) {
        continue;
      }
    }

    // Delete the cookie
    document.cookie = `${name}=; expires=Thu, 01 Jan 1970 00:00:00 UTC; path=${attributes.path || '/'}; domain=${attributes.domain || ''}; secure=${attributes.secure || false}; samesite=${attributes.samesite || 'Lax'}`;
    deletedCount++;
  }

  return deletedCount;
}
```

This function uses the `document.cookie` property to access and manipulate cookies. It splits the cookies string into an array, iterates over each cookie, and checks if it matches the given domain and if its expiration date is older than the threshold. If a cookie meets these criteria, it is deleted by setting its expiration date to a past date.

