```php
<?php

function retrieveUserData(PDO $dbConnection, string $username, int $pageNumber, int $resultsPerPage): array
{
    // Validate and sanitize input parameters
    if (empty($username) || !is_string($username)) {
        throw new InvalidArgumentException("Invalid username parameter");
    }
    if ($pageNumber <= 0 || $resultsPerPage <= 0) {
        throw new InvalidArgumentException("Invalid page number or results per page parameter");
    }

    try {
        // Retrieve foreign key relationship dynamically from the database schema
        $stmt = $dbConnection->query("DESCRIBE users");
        $tableSchema = $stmt->fetchAll(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);
        $foreignKey = "";
        foreach ($tableSchema as $column) {
            if ($column['Key'] === "MUL") {
                $foreignKey = $column['Field'];
                break;
            }
        }
        if (empty($foreignKey)) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Foreign key relationship not found in users table");
        }

        // Prepare and execute the SELECT query with pagination and JOIN
        $offset = ($pageNumber - 1) * $resultsPerPage;
        $stmt = $dbConnection->prepare("
            SELECT users.*, user_details.*
            FROM users
            INNER JOIN user_details ON users.$foreignKey = user_details.$foreignKey
            WHERE users.username = :username
            ORDER BY users.username ASC
            LIMIT :offset, :resultsPerPage
        ");
        $stmt->bindParam(':username', $username, PDO::PARAM_STR);
        $stmt->bindParam(':offset', $offset, PDO::PARAM_INT);
        $stmt->bindParam(':resultsPerPage', $resultsPerPage, PDO::PARAM_INT);
        $stmt->execute();

        // Fetch the retrieved data
        $userData = $stmt->fetchAll(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);

        return $userData;
    } catch (PDOException $e) {
        // Handle database errors
        throw new RuntimeException("Error retrieving data from database: " . $e->getMessage());
    }
}

// Usage example
$dbConnection = new PDO("mysql:host=localhost;dbname=test", "username", "password");
$username = "john_doe";
$pageNumber = 1;
$resultsPerPage = 10;

try {
    $userData = retrieveUserData($dbConnection, $username, $pageNumber, $resultsPerPage);
    var_dump($userData);
} catch (Exception $e) {
    // Handle exceptions and errors
    echo "Error: " . $e->getMessage();
    // Log errors to a file or send error notifications to a specified email address
    error_log($e->getMessage());
}
```

This implementation uses PDO for connecting to the database and handling potential errors by throwing custom exceptions. It also incorporates prepared statements, pagination support, and JOIN queries to retrieve additional information from the "user_details" table based on a foreign key relationship. Input parameters are validated and sanitized, and proper error handling and logging mechanisms are included. The function is designed in a modular and reusable manner, adhering to separation of concerns and proper code organization.

