Here's an example using JavaScript as the programming language:

```javascript
// Example code snippet
const codeSnippet = `
  let myString = 'Hello, world!';
  const myNumber = 42;
  var myBoolean = true;
  const myArray = [1, 2, 3];
  let myObject = { name: 'John', age: 25 };
`;

// Regular expression patterns to extract variable types and values
const variablePattern = /(let|const|var)\s+(\w+)\s*=\s*([^;]+)/g;
const valuePattern = /'([^']*)'|(\d+)|(\[.*?\])|({.*?})/;

// Store the extracted variable types and values
const variables = {};

// Extract variable types and values from the code snippet
let match;
while ((match = variablePattern.exec(codeSnippet))) {
  const [, type, name, value] = match;
  let parsedValue;

  // Parse the value based on its type
  if (value.match(/^{.*}$/)) {
    parsedValue = JSON.parse(value);
  } else if (value.match(/^\[.*\]$/)) {
    parsedValue = JSON.parse(value.replace(/'/g, '"'));
  } else if (value.match(/^'.*'$/)) {
    parsedValue = value.slice(1, -1);
  } else if (value.match(/^\d+$/)) {
    parsedValue = Number(value);
  } else {
    parsedValue = value; // If value type cannot be determined, store it as a string
  }

  // Store the variable type and parsed value
  variables[name] = { type, value: parsedValue };
}

// Output the extracted variable types and values
console.log(variables);
```

This example assumes the code snippet is written in JavaScript. The regular expressions `variablePattern` and `valuePattern` are used to match and extract the variable types and their values, respectively.

The extracted variable types and values are stored in the `variables` object. The value is parsed based on its type: if it matches a regular expression for an object (`{...}`) or an array (`[...]`), it is parsed using `JSON.parse`. If it matches a string pattern (`'...'`), it is extracted without the surrounding quotes. If it matches a number pattern (`\d+`), it is converted to a number. Otherwise, it is stored as a string.

Finally, the extracted variable types and values are outputted using `console.log(variables)`.

