To handle strings with a length greater than 1,000,000 characters efficiently without causing a stack overflow error, the program utilizes tail recursion. In tail recursion, the recursive call is the last operation in the recursive function, so the JVM can optimize it by replacing the current stack frame with a new one, eliminating the need for a new stack frame for each recursive call.

