function fibonacci(n) {
  if (n === 0) {
    return BigInt(0);
  } else if (n === 1) {
    return BigInt(1);
  }

  let prevPrev = BigInt(0);
  let prev = BigInt(1);
  let current = BigInt(0);

  for (let i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
    current = prevPrev + prev;
    prevPrev = prev;
    prev = current;
  }

  return current;
}
```

This function uses a loop to calculate the Fibonacci sequence up to the nth term. It initializes three variables (`prevPrev`, `prev`, and `current`) to keep track of the previous two terms and the current term in the sequence. It starts with the base case for n = 0 and 1, and then iteratively calculates the next term by adding the previous two terms together.

The function uses the `BigInt` type to handle extremely large numbers, as requested. It returns the nth term of the Fibonacci sequence as a `BigInt` to accommodate numbers up to 10^9.

