During the development process, one of the significant challenges faced by the Microsoft Edge team was achieving compatibility with existing web standards while also improving performance and security. A particular challenge was the transition from the older EdgeHTML rendering engine to Chromium, an open-source project by Google that powers many popular web browsers. This transition required adapting the existing codebase and integrating it with the Chromium codebase.

